---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Access Free Tools"
  description="Read the Access Free Tools privacy policy, including browser-first tools, cookies, local preferences, advertising, affiliate links, and user choices."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools is designed to keep browser utilities fast, clear, and privacy-aware.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow legal-copy">
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> April 30, 2026</p>

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This policy explains how Access Free Tools handles information when you use our
      calculators, converters, blog guides, advertising, affiliate links, and other site features.
      It is written for the public website at accessfreetools.com.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser-first tools</h2>
    <p>
      Current tools run in your browser. Calculator history, random number results, and similar
      temporary tool outputs stay in the current browser tab while you use the page and are not
      sent to a server by these tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we may collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not currently offer user accounts or payment checkout on Access Free Tools. We may
      receive basic technical information through hosting, security, browser requests, or future
      analytics tools, such as IP address, browser type, device type, pages visited, referring
      pages, dates, and approximate region. This helps keep the site working, secure, and useful.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the contact form, we receive the name, email address, topic, and message you
      choose to submit. The form sends that message to our site email so we can read it and reply.
      Do not submit passwords, bank details, medical records, or other sensitive personal
      information.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The color look you choose is saved in your browser's local storage so the site can remember
      your preferred style on future visits. You can clear it by clearing site data in your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we add analytics, advertising, affiliate tracking, or consent tools, those services may use
      cookies, web beacons, local storage, IP addresses, device identifiers, or similar technologies.
      You can usually control cookies in your browser settings, but some site features may work less
      smoothly if cookies or local storage are disabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Clipboard actions</h2>
    <p>
      Some tools include copy buttons. These only write the result you choose to your device
      clipboard after you press the copy button.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      We may use Google AdSense or other advertising services to show ads on Access Free Tools.
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits
      to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables Google and its
      partners to serve ads based on visits to this site and other sites on the Internet.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can learn how Google uses data on partner sites at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">
        How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or apps
      </a>. You can opt out of personalized advertising through
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>
      or learn about other industry opt-out choices at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>EEA, UK, and Switzerland consent</h2>
    <p>
      Before serving Google ads to users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or
      Switzerland, we should use a Google-certified Consent Management Platform where required.
      That consent flow should explain the relevant ad technology providers and ask for consent for
      cookies, local storage, and personal data use where the law and Google's EU user consent policy
      require it.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some future blog guides or product callouts may include affiliate links to third-party stores,
      such as print-on-demand products related to a tool. If you click an affiliate link and buy
      something, Access Free Tools may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliate partners
      may use their own cookies or tracking links and handle your information under their own privacy
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
    <p>
      Our pages may link to third-party websites, ad networks, affiliate stores, documentation,
      source references, or product pages. We do not control those third-party services, and their
      privacy practices may be different from ours.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from children
      under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, contact us so we can
      review and remove it where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can clear local storage and cookies in your browser, use the advertising opt-out links
      above, avoid clicking affiliate links, or contact us with privacy questions. If a future form
      asks for personal information, submit only what is needed for that request.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page or email
      <a href="mailto:contact@accessfreetools.com">contact@accessfreetools.com</a>.
      This policy should be reviewed before new analytics, advertising, affiliate, account, or form
      features go live.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
